steps.description:
ServeDNS holds zMu.RLock() for the whole duration of zone.Lookup(ctx, state, qname). When a record is a CNAME pointing outside the configured zone, Lookup calls into Upstream.Lookup, which re-enters the plugin chain and can block on real network I/O. Go's sync.RWMutex blocks new RLock() calls once
```yaml
route53 <SOME_INTERNAL_DOMAIN>.:<SOME_HOSTED_ZONE> {
  fallthrough
}
```
